Fix bubbles that never appear, or appear as garbage

The carousel holds a blank Gtk.Grid at page 0 (the swipe-to-dismiss target)
and the real content at page 1. The scroll_to() in construct is a no-op:
scroll_to needs a real allocation, and the carousel has no size yet. A
toplevel has no allocation at map time either, so a retry there is only
sometimes enough.

When it doesn't land, the bubble stays on the blank page. Two visible
symptoms, same race:

  - the window paints nothing, so the compositor shows whatever was in that
    region of the framebuffer — a rectangle of some other window's content;
  - the carousel settles later and emits page-changed for the placeholder
    page, which on_page_changed reads as a user swipe-to-dismiss, so the
    bubble silently disappears.

Re-assert scroll_to from a tick callback until it lands, and only trust a
page mismatch as a real dismissal once the overlay page has actually been
reached. Reproduced ~3-5 times in 10 with notify-send; 10/10 clean after.

